## Concrete scanner prerequisite blocker

`public.set_updated_at()` is PLpgSQL, resulttrigger, ownerpostgres, SECURITY INVOKER, confignull, no extension/library. Complete stored source:

```sql
begin
  new.updated_at = now();
  return new;
end;
```

BodyMD5 `9b1889f56258bf9d6554213c05019c76`; definitionMD5 `4d6804d5850641a33867814c9e76a714`. Raw/effective EXECUTE ACL is PUBLIC,postgres,anon,authenticated,service_role, all grantorpostgres/non-grantable. Native provenance and full fields are in the saved scanner rows and full function capture. Source migration20260623160506_phase_2_donations_mvp.sql Gitblob8298ff8d908d265dfebc53b98c7b001347c41420 /13500 GitLF bytes /SHAce4831774402e83ef42a3bfcb10bb40ce66b39f94e9ce5b656b9e45327cbd7b2; actual parsed transport13474 bytes /SHAbe2df760ffa4c2dc88fcaa29d72ead4cce665ec9aaab023fd6d4978b3899e4cb. BEFORE UPDATE row triggers connect all nine scoped public tables to this function; auth.users has no such trigger. Scanner ownCoreScope is false because confignull; the actual unchanged conservative operator/call closure refuses the path.

